    {
      "id": "look-closer",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Look closer",
      "position": {
        "x": -430,
        "y": 940
      },
      "width": 470,
      "height": 340,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "navigation",
          "angle": 270
        },
        {
          "id": "next",
          "key": "next",
          "label": "next",
          "direction": "output",
          "dataType": "navigation",
          "angle": 90
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "portId": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "navigation",
          "angle": 270,
          "position": {
            "side": "top",
            "offset": 0.32
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "next",
          "portId": "next",
          "label": "next",
          "direction": "output",
          "dataType": "navigation",
          "angle": 90,
          "position": {
            "side": "bottom",
            "offset": 0.32
          }
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "learn-about-the-graph"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Look closer\n\n**Expand Puppies or Treats.**\n\nWhat looked like one node opens into a complete graph with its own landing content, detail view, summary, icon, and glyph.\n\nNow zoom around before and after expansion. The amount of presentation can change without changing what the thing *is*.\n\nThat is why a large graph does not have to become a wall of tiny boxes."
        },
        "semanticRole": "semantic-zoom-lesson"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "graph-beyond",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "The graph keeps going",
      "position": {
        "x": -430,
        "y": 1380
      },
      "width": 500,
      "height": 330,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "navigation",
          "angle": 270
        },
        {
          "id": "next",
          "key": "next",
          "label": "next",
          "direction": "output",
          "dataType": "navigation",
          "angle": 0
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "portId": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "navigation",
          "angle": 270,
          "position": {
            "side": "top",
            "offset": 0.32
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "next",
          "portId": "next",
          "label": "next",
          "direction": "output",
          "dataType": "navigation",
          "angle": 0,
          "position": {
            "side": "right",
            "offset": 0.5
          }
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "learn-about-the-graph"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# The graph keeps going\n\nPuppies and Treats proved something else: a compact node can stand at the boundary of another graph.\n\nA graph can open into another graph, which can open into another. Detail moves outward without forcing all of it onto one canvas.\n\nThis is much closer to a web than a diagram."
        },
        "semanticRole": "graph-navigation"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lesson-end",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "That's a Twilite graph",
      "position": {
        "x": 360,
        "y": 1380
      },
      "width": 540,
      "height": 350,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "navigation",
          "angle": 180
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "portId": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "navigation",
          "angle": 180,
          "position": {
            "side": "left",
            "offset": 0.5
          }
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "learn-about-the-graph"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# That's a Twilite graph.\n\nYou just explored web content by moving through its structure instead of navigating a stack of pages.\n\nNodes can be content. Relationships carry meaning. Presentation changes with context and zoom. A node can open into another graph.\n\n**The graph isn't a picture of the content. The graph is the content.**"
        },
        "semanticRole": "lesson-conclusion"
      }
    }
  ],
